{% doc %}
  Collection filter form (TE-6 AC2, AC4, AC9, AC10; docs/ui-spec/collection.md §5).
  Reads the global `collection`. Works without JavaScript: the form submits with
  GET and the drawer is a native popover.

  Below 64rem the dialog is the shared `.drawer` (90%, 420 from 48rem), opened by
  collection-filter-open in blocks/collection-products.liquid: header 72 with the
  "Filters" h2 and a close button 48, a body that scrolls on its own, a sticky
  footer with Clear all (only when a filter is applied) and "Show N products".
  From 64rem CSS turns the same dialog into the static left column: no close
  button, no status line; the footer keeps Clear all, and the submit button only
  without JavaScript.

  Layer: `<modal-dialog data-layer="filter">` (ADR 0007, layers.md). Without
  JavaScript the dialog opens as a popover (popovertarget on the open and close
  buttons). With JavaScript, BE (ES1-T110, assets/modal-dialog.js) opens it with
  showModal (remove the popover attribute or close it first: showModal throws on
  an open popover), closes on ×, Esc and the scrim, and returns focus to
  collection-filter-open. "Show N products" closes the drawer when BE has already
  applied the filters. CSS reads [open] and :popover-open the same way.

  The form sits outside the partial so its listeners survive an update. Partial
  collection-filters wraps the status line, the groups and the footer, so the
  "N filters applied · M products" line, "N selected" in each summary, Clear all
  and "Show M products" all update with one refresh. M is collection.products_count
  (after filtering). The sort select in blocks/collection-products.liquid joins
  this form through its form attribute.

  No filters (collection.filters is empty): the dialog stays in the page with
  `hidden`, so the form and the partial still exist and sort still submits. The
  theme editor shows a hint.

  JS hooks: form id collection-filter-form, dialog id collection-filter-drawer,
  on the form data-collection-id (empty on /collections/all; plain id, not a GID),
  data-collection-handle, data-products-count (all_products_count, before
  filtering) for shopify:collection:update (ES1-T104 #6). The form is novalidate:
  a price from the URL above range_max would otherwise block a submit silently
  inside the closed drawer. BE checks min and max before fetching (ES1-T111).
  data-enhanced on <collection-filters> (BE): from 64rem the submit button hides.

  Test hooks: collection-filters (root), collection-filter-drawer,
  collection-filter-close, collection-filter-form, collection-filter-status,
  collection-filter-apply, collection-filter-clear, and the hooks of
  snippets/filter-group.liquid.

  Self-contained: callers must leave the body empty.

  @example
  {% block 'container', id: 'collection-main' %}
    <collection-filters class="collection-layout">
      {% block 'collection-filters' %}{% endblock %}
      {% block 'collection-products' %}{% endblock %}
    </collection-filters>
  {% endblock %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if collection == blank -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="collection-filters__hint" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {{ 'blocks.collection_filters.placeholder' | t }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Same rule as the badge in blocks/collection-products.liquid
    assign active_filter_count = 0
    for filter in collection.filters
      assign active_filter_count = active_filter_count | plus: filter.active_values.size
      if filter.type == 'price_range'
        if filter.min_value.value != nil or filter.max_value.value != nil
          assign active_filter_count = active_filter_count | plus: 1
        endif
      endif
    endfor

    # Clear all keeps a sort order the shopper chose (collection.md §7); the
    # default sort is dropped so the URL has no query (ES1-T109 nojs)
    assign clear_url = collection.url
    if collection.sort_by != blank and collection.sort_by != collection.default_sort_by
      assign sort_param = collection.sort_by | url_encode
      assign clear_url = clear_url | append: '?sort_by=' | append: sort_param
    endif
  -%}

  <div class="collection-filters" data-testid="collection-filters" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- if request.design_mode and collection.filters.size == 0 -%}
      <div class="collection-filters__hint">{{ 'blocks.collection_filters.no_filters' | t }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <modal-dialog data-layer="filter">
      <dialog
        class="drawer collection-filters__drawer"
        id="collection-filter-drawer"
        popover
        aria-labelledby="collection-filter-title"
        data-testid="collection-filter-drawer"
        {% if collection.filters.size == 0 %}
          hidden
        {% endif %}
      >
        <div class="drawer__header collection-filters__header">
          <h2 class="drawer__title collection-filters__title" id="collection-filter-title">
            {{- 'blocks.collection_filters.title' | t -}}
          </h2>
          <button
            class="close-button collection-filters__close"
            type="button"
            popovertarget="collection-filter-drawer"
            popovertargetaction="hide"
            aria-label="{{ 'blocks.collection_filters.close' | t | escape }}"
            data-testid="collection-filter-close"
          >
            {% render 'header-icon', name: 'close' %}
          </button>
        </div>

        <form
          class="collection-filters__form"
          id="collection-filter-form"
          method="get"
          action="{{ collection.url }}"
          novalidate
          data-collection-id="{{ collection.id }}"
          data-collection-handle="{{ collection.handle | escape }}"
          data-products-count="{{ collection.all_products_count }}"
          data-testid="collection-filter-form"
        >
          {% partial 'collection-filters' %}
            {%- liquid
              assign products_label = 'blocks.collection_products.results_count' | t: count: collection.products_count
              assign status_label = products_label
              if active_filter_count > 0
                assign filters_label = 'blocks.collection_products.filters_applied' | t: count: active_filter_count
                assign status_label = 'blocks.collection_filters.status' | t: filters: filters_label, products: products_label
              endif
            -%}
            <div class="collection-filters__panel">
              <div class="drawer__body collection-filters__body">
                <p class="collection-filters__status" role="status" data-testid="collection-filter-status">
                  {{- status_label -}}
                </p>

                <div class="collection-filters__groups">
                  {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
                    {% render 'filter-group', filter: filter %}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="drawer__footer collection-filters__footer">
                {%- if active_filter_count > 0 -%}
                  <a
                    class="button button--secondary collection-filters__clear"
                    href="{{ clear_url }}"
                    data-testid="collection-filter-clear"
                  >
                    {{- 'blocks.collection_filters.clear_all' | t -}}
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}
                <button class="button collection-filters__apply" type="submit" data-testid="collection-filter-apply">
                  {{- 'blocks.collection_filters.show_results' | t: count: collection.products_count -}}
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endpartial %}
        </form>
      </dialog>
    </modal-dialog>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.collection_filters",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
